.TH LUXAFOR-LIGHT 1 "" "luxafor-status" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
luxafor-light \- set the color of a Luxafor USB status light
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B luxafor-light
.I color
.RB [ blink
.RB [ slow | fast ]]
.br
.B luxafor-light off
.br
.B luxafor-light list
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B luxafor-light
drives Luxafor lights (ORB, Flag) directly through their USB HID protocol,
by writing to the light's
.I /dev/hidraw*
device. Every connected light is set to the same color.
.PP
.I color
is a hex code
.RI ( #ff8800 " or " #f80 )
or a CSS color name such as
.BR red ", " orange ", " yellow ", " lime ", " green ", " blue ", " purple .
.PP
With
.BR blink ,
the light blinks in that color by itself (Luxafor "strobe" command) until
the next command;
.B blink slow
and
.B blink fast
change the speed
.RB ( blink\-slow " and " blink\-fast
work too).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B off
Turn the light off.
.TP
.B list
List connected Luxafor lights.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LUXAFOR_BRIGHTNESS
Brightness in percent, 5 to 100 (default: 100).
.TP
.B LUXAFOR_BLINK_SPEED
Blink speed, 1 to 255, lower is faster: overrides
.BR slow / fast ,
to try other speeds.
.TP
.B LUXAFOR_IDS
Space-separated USB
.IR vendor : product
IDs to look for (default: 04d8:f372).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70-luxafor-status.rules
Gives the logged-in user access to the light without sudo.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the light could not be written to, 2 for an unknown
color or effect, 3 if no light is connected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR luxafor-toggle (1),
.BR luxafor-tray (1)
